tag race;

use_tag skate;

// The track: a road that loops along the floor of a canyon. There are a
// few courses, each a canyon of its own; one is built at a time (see
// set_course).
//
// The road's middle line is a smooth closed curve through a few points, kept
// as samples a metre apart. A place on the canyon's floor is known by how
// far along that line it is (s, from the start line, in metres) and how far
// out from it (d, more than 0 to the right of the way round). The road is
// the strip within ROAD_HALF of the line; beyond it lies open ground, fast
// to slow: grass, and at the outside of the bends, sand.
//
// Either side, some way out, stands the canyon's wall, and the walls are
// what a lap is: they have no top, and nothing gets past them, so the floor
// between them is a ring, and the only way to come over the start line
// again is all the way round. Nothing else is checked. The walls stand well
// back from the road (MARGIN or so), so that running wide costs only the
// slower ground; they come nearer only where they must: inside a tight
// bend, and where two stretches of the track pass near each other, with a
// fin of rock left between them.
const ROAD_HALF: f32 = 7.5;

// How far past the road's edge a wall stands, where nothing brings it
// nearer; the least it ever is; and half the thickness of the rock left
// between two stretches.
const MARGIN: f32 = 20.0;

const MIN_MARGIN: f32 = 2.5;

const ROCK_HALF: f32 = 3.0;

// The courses. Each is the points its road's middle line passes through,
// in order, and round again: where (x, z), and how high the road is there
// (the road climbs and falls smoothly from each to the next). A course
// starts along a straight, level or nearly, long enough for the grid behind
// the line; and every course's start line is at the same place, the same
// way round, and (see START_HIGH) as high: it is what stays where it is
// when one course turns into another (see keep_world, in world.l8).
//
// - CANYON RUN: a long straight, down into a hollow, then over a hill, by
//   bends of every kind;
// - SWITCHBACK: up a mountain, a hundred metres and more, by four legs with
//   a hairpin at the end of each; down the other side of it through esses;
//   and over a second hill, with an S down it to the line;
// - ROLLER: short and fast, round and round over dips and crests;
// - TANGLEWOOD: the other way round from the rest, and nowhere straight
//   for long: two hairpins back to back, a chicane, esses, and a kinked run
//   home.
const COURSES: int = 4;

course_names: []str = ["CANYON RUN", "SWITCHBACK", "ROLLER", "TANGLEWOOD"];

course_canyon: []f32 = [-50.0, 0.0, 3.2, 60.0, 0.0, 3.9, 160.0, 6.0, 4.5, 228.0, 40.0,
    0.0, 258.0, 105.0, -9.0, 262.0, 170.0, -14.0, 240.0, 215.0, -10.0, 200.0, 225.0,
    -5.0, 172.0, 195.0, -2.0, 160.0, 150.0, -1.0, 125.0, 105.0, 2.0, 70.0, 95.0, 10.0,
    30.0, 130.0, 20.0, 0.0, 185.0, 26.0, -50.0, 225.0, 18.0, -120.0, 232.0, 6.0, -180.0,
    205.0, -2.0, -214.0, 150.0, -2.6, -196.0, 105.0, -5.2, -212.0, 62.0, -7.8, -208.0,
    25.0, -7.2, -185.0, 4.0, -3.9, -150.0, 0.0, -0.7];

